    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "c99e7c0f-0798-3513-b287-a323f56735b7",
                "word": "hamartia",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "7753976d-f9a4-40d9-9a67-e26159142c44",
                        "entry_id": "c99e7c0f-0798-3513-b287-a323f56735b7",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "hamartias"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "355f55e1-5d59-354d-bfaa-3078e1f88825",
                        "entry_id": "c99e7c0f-0798-3513-b287-a323f56735b7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The tragic flaw of the protagonist in a literary tragedy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Greek",
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c9424c66-c7db-4da9-b835-5ec4bc2f8a71",
                                "sense_id": "355f55e1-5d59-354d-bfaa-3078e1f88825",
                                "text": "Creon's main hamartia was his excessive pride."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "84ad8f39-85e7-4163-ad4f-b5a8d78c099b",
                                "sense_id": "355f55e1-5d59-354d-bfaa-3078e1f88825",
                                "text": "Understanding hamartia as “ignorance of the injurious act,” Lacan distinguishes Greek tragedy from the Renaissance version on the basis that the latter supplants hamartia with the hero's privileged knowledge."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0cd0f9db-6dc3-48b7-bc11-a256a513d131",
                                "sense_id": "355f55e1-5d59-354d-bfaa-3078e1f88825",
                                "text": "The plot and the tragic figure at its center, destroyed through an act of hamartia, should be tailored to the production of pity and fear. Oedipus is not so much a person as he is a hamartia delivery system, a moving, empty center within the motions of the play, who through his vulnerability to hamartia and its disastrous consequences reveals the pitiable and the fearful to the audience."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "07c8458d-dc28-4410-ab29-dabb45956786",
                                "sense_id": "355f55e1-5d59-354d-bfaa-3078e1f88825",
                                "text": "But ever since the concept of \"hamartia\" recurred through Aristotle's Poetics, in an attempt to describe man's ingrained iniquity, our impulse has been to identify a telling defect in those brought suddenly and dramatically low."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a702b0a8-af38-3197-ad1d-b06470ed1698",
                        "entry_id": "c99e7c0f-0798-3513-b287-a323f56735b7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Sin."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b3e94594-3acd-47b6-8124-c391b510b282",
                                "sense_id": "a702b0a8-af38-3197-ad1d-b06470ed1698",
                                "text": "As a consequence of the primeval peripety, the Adamic fall narrated in Genesis 3, they have all inherited the catastrophic and tragic hamartia, as it were, of original sin, the engrained powerlessness of the soul to will the good, much less to do it, along with the deep disorientation of the soul's root desire."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9bd65af6-367c-3cbf-892d-c18dc07d3f61",
                        "entry_id": "c99e7c0f-0798-3513-b287-a323f56735b7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A focal malformation consisting of disorganized arrangement of tissue types."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0fbce81c-3216-4a42-9227-7b209dfccda1",
                        "source_entry_id": "c99e7c0f-0798-3513-b287-a323f56735b7",
                        "source_sense_description": "tragic flaw",
                        "target_lang_word": "hamartia",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hamartia",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ec11b2e7-ba47-3713-885e-f1c02683cab8",
                                        "entry_id": "9c1d510c-1d1e-3177-b794-f7d63a52fa64",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Faute du héros de tragédie qui provoque sa chute."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11a64182-05c4-4105-b07b-568be0380af8",
                                                "sense_id": "ec11b2e7-ba47-3713-885e-f1c02683cab8",
                                                "text": "L’hamartia, selon Aristote, est une faute commise par le héros permettant le renversement du malheur au bonheur ou du bonheur au malheur."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ba8f6e73-8667-3f8e-8abc-f3fd7e56c90c",
                                        "entry_id": "9c1d510c-1d1e-3177-b794-f7d63a52fa64",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Péché dans un contexte grec."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f83b1710-1ce6-4301-9e49-969ce5b15cfe",
                                                "sense_id": "ba8f6e73-8667-3f8e-8abc-f3fd7e56c90c",
                                                "text": "Cette notion de manque est contenue dans le terme grec hamartia, que l’on traduit ordinairement par péché."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "35f3104d-4c39-4bab-9389-9ef3acfc3b96",
                        "source_entry_id": "c99e7c0f-0798-3513-b287-a323f56735b7",
                        "source_sense_description": "tragic flaw",
                        "target_lang_word": "Hamartie",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0916f4ff-f23d-440a-b16c-66a0b8b806b1",
                        "source_entry_id": "c99e7c0f-0798-3513-b287-a323f56735b7",
                        "source_sense_description": "tragic flaw",
                        "target_lang_word": "Irrtum",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Irrtum",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "962ca326-61ef-33a0-8991-ecbe08d48209",
                                        "entry_id": "cb67a1ec-876e-3e79-a103-abf385d0e76f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "unabsichtlich falsche Annahme"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c475c289-6cc9-491e-b81c-2f767e3a0da9",
                                                "sense_id": "962ca326-61ef-33a0-8991-ecbe08d48209",
                                                "text": "Es war ein Irrtum zu denken, dass hier schon ein Beispiel steht."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6fb6d04d-c56c-4b2e-95e9-fb5ea093787b",
                                                "sense_id": "962ca326-61ef-33a0-8991-ecbe08d48209",
                                                "text": "„Jedenfalls mag ich es, wenn sich kurz oder lange in mir aufbewahrte Irrtümer in nichts als Wohlgefallen auflösen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "945ea0bd-697b-4fb4-b642-64d3ecd91b43",
                                                "sense_id": "962ca326-61ef-33a0-8991-ecbe08d48209",
                                                "text": "„Ein weitverbreiteter Irrtum, dem besonders gerne intellektuelle Trinker anhängen, die ihre Exzesse akademisch rechtfertigen wollen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab0d0f7f-cc4c-4791-bc43-dbc0adcde08d",
                                                "sense_id": "962ca326-61ef-33a0-8991-ecbe08d48209",
                                                "text": "„Dieses Mal war kein Irrtum mehr möglich.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "adf4d42f-c3fb-489a-a7eb-e82476111f0c",
                                                "sense_id": "962ca326-61ef-33a0-8991-ecbe08d48209",
                                                "text": "„Ihr neuer Freund war im Irrtum gewesen, sie hatte in Wahrheit nie gezögert.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
